<title>CANADA: CWB details primary elevator space.</title>
<headline>CWB details primary elevator space.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>There was more space available Tuesday in primary elevators across Canada's Prairies compared to a week earlier, the Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>Vacant country elevator space rose to 37 percent in Alberta compared to 30 percent the week before, CWB spokeswoman Rhea Yates said.</p>
<p>Space in Saskatchewan rose to 24 percent compared to 20 percent the prior week, Yates said.</p>
<p>Manitoba elevators had 18 percent of space vacant compared to 17 percent the week before, she said.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
